From c47abcf0454624138652e49f0061aaa1b8ea1185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:18:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: IOP clock follows the EE clock; click-free SPU output
 queue

The IOP ran ~0.9% ahead of EE time / 8 (0.7% from cycles run outside
runEeCycles, e.g. synchronous RPC waits, 0.2% from slice overshoot), so the
SPU produced ~48420 samples per real second and the output queue cut the
excess every few seconds: audible pops in voices. runEeCycles now repays
the IOP's lead (capped at kMaxIopLeadCycles) instead of adding to it.

SpuPcmQueue: proportional + integral rate control, crossfaded skip past a
500 ms backlog instead of hard drops, fade-out/refill/fade-in on underrun.
GA2_PERF [audio] line reports producer/consumer rates, drift and skips.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
